  "central_principle": "Drought reduces photosynthesis through interacting hydraulic, stomatal, biochemical, photochemical, oxidative, and carbon-transport limitations. Stomatal limitation usually dominates during mild-to-moderate drought, whereas direct damage to chloroplast and cellular function becomes more important under severe or prolonged drought.",
  "causal_sequence": [
    "Soil drying lowers plant and leaf water potential.",
    "Hydraulic and hormonal signals, especially abscisic acid, promote stomatal closure.",
