  "content_outline": [
    {
      "topic": "1. From deterministic change to random change",
      "explanation": "An ordinary differential equation such as dX/dt = μ describes a unique path when the initial value is known. An SDE adds a continuously fluctuating term. The randomness is not represented by assigning a new random value at every isolated step; instead, it is accumulated through infinitely many small independent Brownian increments."
