    {
      "topic": "2. Wiener-process foundation",
      "properties": [
        "W_0 = 0.",
        "The increment W_t − W_s is normally distributed with mean 0 and variance t − s.",
        "Disjoint increments are independent.",
        "W_t is almost surely continuous but nowhere differentiable.",
        "The process has quadratic variation [W]_t = t."
      ],
      "small_increment_approximation": "W_(t+Δt) − W_t ≈ √Δt Z, where Z has the standard normal distribution."
