      "topic": "3. Standard scalar SDE",
      "equation": "dX_t = μ(X_t,t)dt + σ(X_t,t)dW_t",
      "integral_form": "X_t = X_0 + ∫₀ᵗ μ(X_s,s)ds + ∫₀ᵗ σ(X_s,s)dW_s",
      "interpretation": [
        "The drift integral describes cumulative systematic change.",
        "The stochastic integral describes cumulative random change.",
        "The parameter μ has units of state per unit time.",
        "The parameter σ has units of state per square-root time because W_t has units of square-root time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "4. Itô calculus",
      "ito_algebra": [
        "dt² is negligible to first order.",
        "dt dW is negligible to first order.",
        "The effective rule is (dW)² = dt."
